Micro-UAVs have a fundamental payload limitation that is difficult to overcome in many practical applications. However, larger payloads can be manipulated and transported by multiple UAVs either using grippers (Mellinger et al., 2010b) or cables (Michael et al., 2011a). Applications such as surveillance that require imagery from multiple sensors can be addressed by coordinating multiple UAVs, each with
